## 6. Residual (not this cycle)

  These facts stay residual. They are not `[ ]` work unless the owner names one.
  Public install is the checkout XDG installer (`ooda install`). First machine clones https://github.com/openOODA/ooda, then gcc + seed rebuild.
  HITL is not product. The human loop is `ooda fix`.
  vscode still talks to `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js`.
  `qa/e2e/*.sh` and the broken fixtures named in the `qa_master.oo` header stay residual. `qa_master.oo` is product (22 green).
  `import ".h"` still refuses. `import_c(...)` and `lto_xlang_link` are product (OPEN-70).
  AArch64 product-ELF dispatch is residual. Side emit-aarch64 hello .s + clang assemble is a named lock (`scripts/aarch64_hello_smoke.oo`). Link and qemu run stay residual. Standalone x86_64 `emit-x86` is product (OPEN-69).
  Dummy WASM `end` stays on non-print functions. Print-lit, hello greet fold, same-fn ident-let, N-string const strcat, two-println, three-println, int-lit println, const INT+INT, if-true/if-false, if-true-no-else, and if INT==INT are named locks. Mixed ident concat stays dummy. Hostile second print stays dummy. IDENT if stays dummy. IDENT add stays dummy. IDENT third print, extra stmt beside no-else, and if 1==x stay dummy. Extra emit-wasm writes `\0asm`. A browser WASM host is residual. Not a complete WASM backend.
  Device GPU dispatch is residual. `emit_ptx` text is product (OPEN-91).
  SGX / TDX / SEV hardware enclaves are residual. Measured isolate is product (OPEN-74).
  Full general symbolic SMT is residual. Const header `requires` / `ensures` / `spec` fold is product (OPEN-81).
  Inventory door: `audit/library_status.oot` (each sibling <= 256).

